        "Substitute $a = x + x^2$ into the expansion from part (a):\n$$(1 + x + x^2)^5 = 1 + 5(x + x^2) + 10(x + x^2)^2 + 10(x + x^2)^3 + \\dots$$",
        "Expand the polynomial terms keeping powers up to $x^3$:\n$$5(x + x^2) = 5x + 5x^2$$\n$$10(x + x^2)^2 = 10(x^2 + 2x^3 + x^4) = 10x^2 + 20x^3 + \\dots$$\n$$10(x + x^2)^3 = 10(x^3 + \\dots) = 10x^3 + \\dots$$",
        "Combine all terms of like degree:\n$$(1 + x + x^2)^5 = 1 + 5x + (5 + 10)x^2 + (20 + 10)x^3 = 1 + 5x + 15x^2 + 30x^3$$"
